WEBVTT

00:01.901 --> 00:06.481
Lucie girl! Little bird!
You're up so high!

00:06.611 --> 00:08.531
[squealing]

00:08.651 --> 00:10.951
[RUDEUS] She is so cute!

00:11.071 --> 00:13.031
There's nothing
in the entire world

00:13.161 --> 00:16.201
that's more adorable
than my little baby girl.

00:16.331 --> 00:19.831
I didn't know angels were real
until I met her.

00:19.961 --> 00:21.711
-[SUZANNE] You know...
-Hmm?

00:21.831 --> 00:23.421
...your wife hired me
to wet nurse,

00:23.541 --> 00:25.091
so I can take her any time.

00:25.211 --> 00:27.171
Come on, Suzanne,
she's my daughter.

00:27.301 --> 00:29.341
I wanna play with her.
But thanks, I guess.

00:29.471 --> 00:32.851
Sure. If you insist,
then go ahead.

00:32.971 --> 00:35.101
What father
wouldn't want to, seriously?

00:35.221 --> 00:38.181
My husband would've turned
and run away already.

00:38.311 --> 00:41.601
Hmm. Timothy's not big
on fatherhood, eh?

00:43.151 --> 00:45.061
-[Lucie squeals]
-Hey, Lucie.

00:45.191 --> 00:47.231
Huh. You're a funny one.

00:47.361 --> 00:50.071
Anyway, I couldn't believe it
when Sylphie said your name.

00:50.191 --> 00:51.861
I had no idea
you'd moved to Sharia.

00:51.991 --> 00:53.571
Hmm. Yeah, back at you.

00:53.701 --> 00:55.701
I was shocked to hear
you were married with a baby.

00:55.831 --> 00:57.491
You didn't really seem
like the type.

00:57.621 --> 00:58.621
Yeah.

00:58.751 --> 01:01.001
So Counter Arrow
has split up entirely?

01:01.121 --> 01:02.291
Yeah,

01:02.421 --> 01:05.001
a little while
after we parted ways with you.

01:05.131 --> 01:07.551
Losing a member
really takes a toll,

01:07.671 --> 01:09.761
especially true
up at those higher ranks.

01:09.881 --> 01:11.011
Mm.

01:12.591 --> 01:14.511
So, uh, what about Sara?

01:14.641 --> 01:16.391
You really wanna know?

01:16.511 --> 01:17.851
I mean, sure.

01:18.681 --> 01:21.061
She's still out adventuring
with another party.

01:21.181 --> 01:22.231
Hmm.

01:22.771 --> 01:24.101
[SUZANNE]
If you wanna talk to her,

01:24.231 --> 01:25.651
I can put you in touch.

01:25.771 --> 01:29.281
It's a dangerous profession,
and accidents happen, so...

01:30.361 --> 01:34.201
No, I don't think I have much
of anything to say.

01:35.161 --> 01:36.701
That's all right.

01:37.831 --> 01:39.951
[LILIA] Pardon me,
Master Rudeus.

01:40.081 --> 01:41.201
Just checking in.

01:41.331 --> 01:42.961
Her ladyship
seemed a little concerned

01:43.081 --> 01:44.581
about young Miss Lucie.

01:44.711 --> 01:45.711
Hey, Mom.

01:46.251 --> 01:48.501
She's as happy and healthy
as ever.

01:51.381 --> 01:52.511
[squealing]

01:53.011 --> 01:56.341
Lucie-goosey loves her grandma,
don't you?

01:57.551 --> 01:58.851
Hmm?

02:02.061 --> 02:03.351
[whimpers]

02:03.771 --> 02:04.731
[crying]

02:04.851 --> 02:08.111
Oh, Master Rudeus, may I?

02:10.781 --> 02:13.111
Oh, my word, what's the matter?

02:13.611 --> 02:15.661
Did you make a mess
in your diaper?

02:16.571 --> 02:17.531
Hmm.

02:17.661 --> 02:19.581
Yeah, probably just hungry.

02:21.241 --> 02:22.411
[gasps]

02:22.961 --> 02:26.581
Did Mom just intuit
Lucie's feeding time?

02:27.791 --> 02:30.631
I'll take that as another sign
that she's recovering.

02:32.341 --> 02:34.511
[♪ opening theme song playing]

02:39.141 --> 02:41.141
[yawns]

02:41.721 --> 02:43.271
Early, I know.

02:43.391 --> 02:45.351
Thank you
for agreeing to come with us.

02:45.481 --> 02:48.271
Absolutely.
I'd never say no to you.

02:48.401 --> 02:52.441
Not to the mage handpicked
to guard the princess of Ranoa.

02:52.571 --> 02:53.611
It's an honor.

02:54.031 --> 02:56.651
[ROXY] Stop.
I wasn't "handpicked."

02:56.781 --> 02:59.661
[RUDEUS] Apparently, members
of the Ranoan royal family

02:59.781 --> 03:02.541
are expected to make a sort of
coming-of-age pilgrimage

03:02.661 --> 03:04.121
around the country.

03:04.961 --> 03:06.121
It's nothing too strenuous,

03:06.251 --> 03:08.331
just a tour
of important landmarks,

03:08.461 --> 03:11.421
but they have to arrange for
their own travel and protection.

03:12.171 --> 03:15.011
And you're filling in
for some other adventurer

03:15.131 --> 03:16.471
from her regular detail?

03:16.591 --> 03:19.091
[ROXY] Right. One of
their party members fell ill,

03:19.221 --> 03:20.141
so...

03:20.591 --> 03:21.801
And Sylphie said that

03:21.931 --> 03:24.021
Princess Ariel
is coming as well.

03:24.141 --> 03:25.221
Yes, because she wants

03:25.391 --> 03:27.691
to establish a connection
to the Ranoan family.

03:27.811 --> 03:29.311
[RUDEUS]
She's willing to traipse

03:29.441 --> 03:30.981
through
a monster-infested forest

03:31.111 --> 03:32.231
just to network?

03:32.361 --> 03:34.111
I'm honestly impressed.

03:34.611 --> 03:36.611
[ROXY] Well, that makes
one of us, I suppose.

03:36.741 --> 03:38.821
I was nervous enough
to begin with,

03:38.951 --> 03:42.121
and having to guard two royals
now instead of just one...

03:42.241 --> 03:43.781
-[sighs]
-[Rudeus chuckles]

03:44.371 --> 03:46.621
But that's why we thought
to ask you along too.

03:46.751 --> 03:48.211
So thanks again for coming.

03:48.871 --> 03:50.791
[RUDEUS] Yeah.
You know I've got your back.

03:51.381 --> 03:52.671
[ROXY] I'm counting on it.

03:54.591 --> 03:58.971
MUSHOKU TENSEI
JOBLESS REINCARNATION III

04:01.391 --> 04:04.101
[RANOAN PRINCESS] My! So you
must do the same here in Asura.

04:04.221 --> 04:05.141
[ARIEL] Indeed.

04:05.431 --> 04:07.851
Many of our gardens
are inside the palace walls.

04:07.981 --> 04:09.441
I suppose
with the weather you get here,

04:09.561 --> 04:11.021
I shouldn't be surprised.

04:11.151 --> 04:12.901
[giggles] Sounds lovely.

04:14.311 --> 04:15.861
Hail and well met.

04:15.981 --> 04:17.191
Names, please?

04:17.321 --> 04:18.361
Yes, of course.

04:18.491 --> 04:21.241
My name is
Roxy Migurdia Greyrat.

04:21.361 --> 04:22.911
I'm Rudeus Greyrat.

04:23.371 --> 04:24.451
Dame Grace,

04:25.081 --> 04:26.541
pardon my intrusion.

04:26.661 --> 04:28.461
These are the two mages
who will be joining us

04:28.581 --> 04:29.661
on duty this morning.

04:30.371 --> 04:31.331
[GRACE] Ah.

04:31.461 --> 04:33.041
So you're the ones.

04:33.541 --> 04:35.461
Sylphiette told me.

04:35.591 --> 04:37.551
I'm Grace, a royal knight.

04:37.961 --> 04:39.471
We're glad to have you.

04:39.921 --> 04:40.931
[RUDEUS] I understand we're here

04:41.051 --> 04:43.221
to support
some other adventurers?

04:43.341 --> 04:46.561
A freelance party
called Amazon Ace.

04:46.681 --> 04:48.891
I expect their return
any moment now.

04:49.021 --> 04:50.441
[WOMAN 1] I'm not
going to tell you again!

04:50.561 --> 04:52.101
[WOMAN 2] Okay,
so am I the only one

04:52.231 --> 04:53.771
who remembers
what happened last time?

04:53.901 --> 04:55.981
Where Tina and Melanie
literally almost died

04:56.111 --> 04:57.571
because we didn't stick
to the plan?

04:57.691 --> 04:59.531
I don't want
to have any part in this!

04:59.651 --> 05:00.821
[WOMAN 1]
What do you want me to do?

05:00.951 --> 05:02.361
We're not calling
the shots here.

05:02.491 --> 05:03.531
[WOMAN 2] I'd rather work alone

05:03.661 --> 05:05.201
than have to rely
on some random stranger

05:05.331 --> 05:06.281
to watch my back.

05:06.621 --> 05:08.831
Look, you can't be the only one
on the back line.

05:08.951 --> 05:10.751
And if the random stranger's
a team player,

05:10.871 --> 05:12.171
they've already got
a leg up on you.

05:12.291 --> 05:14.291
[WOMAN 3] Yeah.
You've gotta learn to work

05:14.421 --> 05:16.131
with whoever you get
teamed up with.

05:16.251 --> 05:17.801
It may not seem important now,

05:17.921 --> 05:19.051
but we don't really
get the luxury

05:19.171 --> 05:21.381
of hanging
with the same party forever.

05:21.511 --> 05:22.471
Uh.

05:23.261 --> 05:24.641
[gasps softly]

05:25.261 --> 05:26.811
[gasps]

05:28.521 --> 05:29.601
Unbelievable.

05:29.721 --> 05:31.731
What? Do you know that guy?

05:31.851 --> 05:33.151
Um, yeah.

05:37.651 --> 05:38.731
[RUDEUS] Sara.

05:38.861 --> 05:40.231
It's been a long time,

05:40.361 --> 05:42.781
but I couldn't forget her
if I tried.

05:43.111 --> 05:44.401
She's brash,

05:44.531 --> 05:45.871
she's combative,

05:45.991 --> 05:47.621
she's brilliant.

05:48.201 --> 05:49.871
She and her party invited me out

05:50.001 --> 05:51.121
for a bunch of jobs together,

05:51.251 --> 05:53.791
and eventually,
she took a liking to me.

05:53.911 --> 05:55.631
And I, well...

05:56.501 --> 05:58.921
I never really figured out
how I felt about her.

05:59.041 --> 06:00.711
I tried,

06:00.841 --> 06:03.261
but things escalated
before I could be sure,

06:03.381 --> 06:05.341
and then I messed up.

06:06.091 --> 06:07.431
So, it ended.

06:07.551 --> 06:08.811
And I was pretty sure

06:08.931 --> 06:11.061
I was never
going to see her again.

06:12.021 --> 06:13.731
I was very sure.

06:14.271 --> 06:17.101
[grunts] Alyssa! Sara!

06:17.231 --> 06:18.821
Handle those two, would ya?

06:19.611 --> 06:22.441
Let the great protection of fire
converge where thou seekest!

06:23.071 --> 06:25.151
I call forth the bold heat
of a torch here and now!

06:25.281 --> 06:26.951
Firefall!

06:28.241 --> 06:29.331
[roars]

06:29.451 --> 06:30.371
[both gasp]

06:30.491 --> 06:31.791
[ROXY] May this smoldering spark

06:31.911 --> 06:33.791
call forth a great
and searing blessing!

06:33.911 --> 06:35.331
Flamethrower!

06:44.801 --> 06:46.131
Wow.

06:46.591 --> 06:47.721
[sighs]

06:48.341 --> 06:50.221
[gasps]

06:50.351 --> 06:52.431
[ROXY] Do you need
anything from me?

06:52.561 --> 06:53.681
No, we're okay.

06:53.811 --> 06:54.941
[gasps]

07:05.111 --> 07:07.201
Ah, I'll be damned.

07:07.321 --> 07:09.871
Yeah, they took out
those monsters quick.

07:09.991 --> 07:10.951
There were those rumors

07:11.201 --> 07:13.371
that a teacher cleared
the Teleporter Labyrinth.

07:13.501 --> 07:15.331
I guess that was true after all.

07:15.461 --> 07:17.581
The way you balance
offensive and healing magic

07:17.711 --> 07:19.041
is so impressive to me!

07:19.171 --> 07:20.751
It's such a clean,
simple theory,

07:20.881 --> 07:22.881
and you put it
into practice so elegantly!

07:23.001 --> 07:24.591
Wow, you don't say!

07:24.711 --> 07:26.631
What happened to, "I can't
believe they just stuck me

07:26.761 --> 07:28.471
on the back line
with some little kid"?

07:28.591 --> 07:30.681
You look young!
Please forgive me!

07:30.801 --> 07:33.511
[ROXY] Oh, that's okay.
It happens all the time.

07:33.641 --> 07:35.351
[RUDEUS] Warms me
right up inside

07:35.471 --> 07:36.811
to see people treating Roxy

07:36.941 --> 07:38.651
with the reverence she deserves.

07:38.771 --> 07:40.151
[chuckles]

07:40.271 --> 07:41.521
That's my master.

07:41.651 --> 07:43.401
[chuckles, gasps]

07:46.861 --> 07:49.071
Okay, we need
to get some food going

07:49.201 --> 07:50.781
before the princesses return
from the shrine.

07:50.911 --> 07:51.871
Uh, listen, Rudeus--

07:52.031 --> 07:53.701
I'd be happy to take care
of the cooking,

07:53.831 --> 07:55.791
since I'm not as much use
on the battlefield.

07:55.911 --> 07:57.581
[WOMAN] You? I don't know.

07:57.711 --> 07:58.661
[RUDEUS] I know I don't look it,

07:58.791 --> 08:00.791
but I know my way
around a fire, trust me.

08:00.921 --> 08:03.001
So, she used to be his woman?

08:03.631 --> 08:05.961
Did he ever tell you
what happened between them?

08:06.091 --> 08:08.261
No, but I've got a general idea.

08:09.931 --> 08:11.721
[LUKE] Well, we may
run into another pack

08:11.841 --> 08:13.011
of monsters on our way home,

08:13.141 --> 08:15.181
so I'd like
to have everyone focused.

08:15.311 --> 08:16.641
...just let me know.

08:18.601 --> 08:21.771
The service at the shrine
went smoothly, I trust?

08:21.901 --> 08:22.811
Very.

08:22.941 --> 08:24.611
I'm grateful for your company.

08:24.731 --> 08:27.191
I can finish my pilgrimage here
in luxury.

08:27.321 --> 08:28.821
I'm delighted to hear it.

08:28.951 --> 08:31.991
Auntie Roxy! Would you mind
teaching me some new magic

08:32.121 --> 08:33.411
on our journey back?

08:33.531 --> 08:34.831
Sure, if you want me to.

08:34.951 --> 08:36.041
[gasps] Hooray!

08:36.161 --> 08:38.041
-Thanks, Auntie Roxy!
-[fuming]

08:38.161 --> 08:40.541
[ROXY] Um, you don't have to
call me that, though.

08:41.501 --> 08:44.461
[RUDEUS] Okay, now I'm starting
to get a little jealous.

08:44.591 --> 08:46.541
Roxy's getting
such a warm reception!

08:46.671 --> 08:47.961
I wanna join the fun.

08:48.091 --> 08:50.511
I could be Papa Rudy
or something.

08:50.631 --> 08:53.051
-Rudy, have you talked?
-[gasps]

08:54.391 --> 08:56.311
You should
at least say something.

08:56.431 --> 08:59.141
Yeah, I know I should, but...

09:00.231 --> 09:03.061
[ARIEL] Goodness,
my throat is simply parched.

09:04.191 --> 09:07.441
I spied some gorgeous
yellow fruit along our path.

09:07.571 --> 09:09.491
It feels terribly selfish
to ask,

09:09.611 --> 09:11.611
but I would love
to have a taste.

09:11.741 --> 09:13.451
Could I trouble you
to fetch me one?

09:13.571 --> 09:14.571
[SARA] Mm?

09:17.451 --> 09:19.831
Yeah, you got it. I'm on my way.

09:20.371 --> 09:21.661
Well, I certainly can't approve

09:21.791 --> 09:23.961
of you walking
through the forest alone.

09:24.081 --> 09:25.881
Say, Rudeus, Fitz,

09:26.001 --> 09:28.091
do accompany her,
would you kindly?

09:28.631 --> 09:32.341
[RUDEUS] Huh. Is she just trying
to be considerate?

09:32.471 --> 09:34.341
Well, at least
Sylphie will be there.

09:34.471 --> 09:36.301
[SYLPHIETTE] Rudy will be enough
to accompany her.

09:37.721 --> 09:39.931
I would prefer
to remain at your side.

09:40.061 --> 09:41.891
Are you certain?

09:42.021 --> 09:42.941
[SYLPHIETTE] Oh, yes.

09:43.481 --> 09:45.481
He won't hide from danger.

09:48.691 --> 09:51.571
[RUDEUS] Is that what
I've been doing? Hiding?

09:56.031 --> 09:58.581
Can't keep that up forever,
now can I?

09:59.291 --> 10:02.121
Then it's settled.
Take care, Rudeus.

10:04.161 --> 10:05.211
Right.

10:18.681 --> 10:20.931
So, you, uh,
stuck with adventuring.

10:21.721 --> 10:23.181
[SARA] What's that
supposed to mean?

10:24.851 --> 10:27.021
It's just that
Counter Arrow split up,

10:27.151 --> 10:29.111
and Suzanne and Timothy
got married,

10:29.231 --> 10:30.651
so they quit adventuring.

10:31.361 --> 10:32.861
And Patrice went back to Asura

10:32.991 --> 10:35.741
to become a soldier
or something, I heard?

10:39.201 --> 10:40.831
[♪ gentle music playing]

10:40.951 --> 10:42.581
But you've been all right?

10:42.701 --> 10:44.871
[SARA] I bounced around
to a bunch of different parties.

10:45.961 --> 10:48.881
I've been with this one
ever since I hit rank A, though.

10:49.001 --> 10:51.751
[RUDEUS] I don't think I've ever
seen an all-women party before.

10:52.551 --> 10:55.171
[SARA] Yeah, they're actually
pretty common at low ranks,

10:55.301 --> 10:57.761
but you kind of stop seeing them
above rank C

10:57.891 --> 11:00.601
because the pros are all looking
for skill over gender.

11:01.261 --> 11:02.271
[RUDEUS] Yeah.

11:02.891 --> 11:05.271
[SARA] This is the first time
I've been in one myself.

11:05.771 --> 11:07.441
But it's definitely
got its perks.

11:08.021 --> 11:10.061
Some clients
actually prefer us for it.

11:10.611 --> 11:12.361
[RUDEUS]
You are pretty well-suited

11:12.481 --> 11:13.651
for guarding a princess.

11:13.781 --> 11:15.071
That's for sure.

11:16.491 --> 11:18.531
It's less stressful overall.

11:18.661 --> 11:21.701
Way fewer doomed
inter-party love affairs.

11:22.241 --> 11:23.331
[gasps]

11:25.871 --> 11:27.161
[laughs awkwardly]

11:27.291 --> 11:28.501
[chuckles]

11:29.001 --> 11:30.631
I hear you've been good.

11:31.131 --> 11:32.291
Uh, from who?

11:32.421 --> 11:34.211
I heard it from Suzanne,
that's who.

11:34.341 --> 11:36.221
She says you're married
to two wives,

11:36.341 --> 11:37.421
with a baby and a house,

11:37.551 --> 11:38.931
and you're living the dream.

11:39.051 --> 11:40.511
Yeah, I guess I kind of am.

11:41.801 --> 11:42.851
Sorry.

11:43.011 --> 11:46.181
I don't need an apology
about it! [huffs]

11:58.611 --> 11:59.781
[gasps]

12:05.331 --> 12:06.501
Sara.

12:07.121 --> 12:11.331
You may not need to hear it,
but I need... to say it.

12:11.831 --> 12:15.711
We, um... We didn't exactly
part on great terms,

12:15.841 --> 12:19.971
so this morning, I just kind of
freaked out when I saw you.

12:20.091 --> 12:22.931
But still,
it was wrong to avoid you.

12:23.511 --> 12:24.561
I'm sorry.

12:25.561 --> 12:26.851
[SARA] Whatever.

12:26.971 --> 12:29.691
I don't need you
to feel sorry for me, okay?

12:31.311 --> 12:32.441
[RUDEUS] Can I sit with you?

12:32.811 --> 12:35.521
[SARA] As long as it's not
going to upset your wives.

12:35.651 --> 12:37.191
[Rudeus chuckles] Trust me,
they're gonna hear

12:37.321 --> 12:39.071
all about this
as soon as we're back.

12:39.191 --> 12:43.571
Oh. The white-haired bodyguard,
she's one of them, isn't she?

12:43.701 --> 12:45.911
Yeah.
I thought Suzanne told you.

12:46.031 --> 12:48.411
Well, it's not like she gave me
all the details.

12:49.371 --> 12:51.581
She's pretty. You're lucky.

12:51.711 --> 12:55.171
And Roxy, the blue-haired mage
that's with us.

12:55.291 --> 12:57.091
Whoa, whole family's here.

12:57.211 --> 12:58.341
This Roxy,

12:58.461 --> 13:00.841
is she the same Roxy
who taught you magic?

13:00.971 --> 13:01.971
Yeah.

13:02.091 --> 13:03.301
Huh.

13:09.561 --> 13:10.851
You know,

13:10.981 --> 13:14.271
I've felt like I owed you
an apology all this time.

13:14.401 --> 13:15.771
[RUDEUS] No. What?

13:15.901 --> 13:16.861
Why?

13:17.401 --> 13:19.901
[SARA] Mm. It wasn't
until after we split up

13:20.031 --> 13:21.901
that I found out
that you were...

13:22.031 --> 13:23.661
you know, sick.

13:25.321 --> 13:27.491
I got all mad
and pitched a big fit,

13:27.621 --> 13:32.251
but... I didn't stop to think
that you might be hurting too.

13:35.831 --> 13:38.511
If I could have just
been an adult about it,

13:39.301 --> 13:42.511
I might have realized
that you were in an awful place.

13:42.681 --> 13:43.841
So...

13:45.091 --> 13:46.641
I'm sorry too.

13:49.811 --> 13:52.431
I said some pretty mean stuff,

13:52.561 --> 13:55.441
but recently, I realized

13:55.561 --> 13:58.231
that was all way more about me
than it was you.

13:58.361 --> 13:59.941
What made that click?

14:00.401 --> 14:02.701
I was really attached
to someone,

14:02.821 --> 14:04.861
this girl called Eris.

14:04.991 --> 14:07.071
I thought
that she'd abandoned me.

14:07.871 --> 14:09.991
So when you developed
feelings for me,

14:10.121 --> 14:13.621
I felt like I had an opening
to move on, you know?

14:13.751 --> 14:16.001
Put all that in the past.

14:16.131 --> 14:18.671
You saw how that worked out,
of course,

14:18.791 --> 14:21.381
but I didn't want that
to be my fault again,

14:22.051 --> 14:23.471
so I lashed out

14:23.591 --> 14:25.391
and said some horrible stuff.

14:26.011 --> 14:28.511
You have nothing
to apologize for.

14:29.261 --> 14:31.471
Look at you. You grew up.

14:31.601 --> 14:32.851
You think?

14:32.981 --> 14:33.891
Mm-hmm.

14:33.981 --> 14:35.691
The old you
never would have opened up

14:35.811 --> 14:37.691
about his feelings so easily.

14:38.191 --> 14:39.771
And he wouldn't
have been so casual

14:39.901 --> 14:41.321
with me about it, either.

14:41.441 --> 14:42.861
[RUDEUS] She's right.

14:43.321 --> 14:44.321
I tried pretty hard

14:44.531 --> 14:46.531
to keep people
at arm's length back then.

14:47.111 --> 14:48.411
I was scared

14:48.531 --> 14:49.911
of being hated,

14:50.031 --> 14:51.751
of not being good enough,

14:51.871 --> 14:53.541
of being rejected again.

14:54.121 --> 14:55.411
But now...

14:55.541 --> 14:57.251
I've picked up some confidence.

14:57.381 --> 14:58.921
From your wives?

14:59.041 --> 15:01.501
Yeah. Sylphie was
really patient with me

15:01.631 --> 15:04.261
about my whole condition,
thankfully.

15:04.721 --> 15:06.131
She had never, um,

15:06.261 --> 15:09.101
but she really
committed herself.

15:09.221 --> 15:11.601
She used aphrodisiacs, uh...

15:11.721 --> 15:14.891
Wow. Sounds like
she's really dedicated to you.

15:15.021 --> 15:16.641
That's something else.

15:16.771 --> 15:17.731
Hang on.

15:17.851 --> 15:19.561
You mean
she did all that for you,

15:19.691 --> 15:21.441
and you still
married a second time?

15:21.571 --> 15:23.151
[chuckles]
When you say it like that...

15:23.941 --> 15:26.401
But Roxy kind of
did the same thing for me.

15:27.201 --> 15:30.951
My dad died on a quest,
and I just kind of shut down,

15:31.071 --> 15:33.951
and it was Roxy
who pulled me out of it.

15:34.661 --> 15:35.751
Oh, wow.

15:38.921 --> 15:41.211
Well, I couldn't have done that.

15:41.841 --> 15:43.251
Even with all the context,

15:43.381 --> 15:45.511
I don't think I'd have been
that much help.

15:45.631 --> 15:47.131
And that said,

15:47.261 --> 15:48.801
it's no wonder
I couldn't get you

15:48.931 --> 15:50.551
to fall for me then, is it?

15:54.181 --> 15:55.481
[RUDEUS] I guess not.

15:55.851 --> 15:58.021
Sylphie and Roxy both love me,

15:58.141 --> 15:59.771
but I love them more.

16:00.271 --> 16:02.481
They won my heart
by being there for me.

16:03.271 --> 16:05.361
Maybe that's
what sets them apart.

16:05.481 --> 16:06.691
They changed my life.

16:08.281 --> 16:09.661
[Sara grunts]

16:10.991 --> 16:13.951
All righty, then.
I am over it, by the way.

16:14.081 --> 16:16.621
I don't still have feelings
for you or anything.

16:16.751 --> 16:18.911
Though, I'm glad
I got to apologize

16:19.041 --> 16:21.751
because I said some awful stuff
way back then.

16:21.881 --> 16:23.001
But that's it.

16:23.501 --> 16:25.211
I don't wanna try and start
something up again

16:25.341 --> 16:26.671
is all I'm saying.

16:26.801 --> 16:29.131
-Okay? We're good.
-Uh...

16:29.261 --> 16:31.641
So don't you
keep feeling bad about it.

16:32.721 --> 16:36.431
We're just former comrades,
and I guess current ones.

16:40.691 --> 16:42.771
Okay. Sounds good.

16:46.111 --> 16:48.151
[♪ dramatic music playing]

16:49.441 --> 16:51.031
[grunts]

16:53.281 --> 16:54.321
[slashes]

16:55.621 --> 16:56.911
[both gasp]

16:58.621 --> 17:00.291
[gasps]

17:01.211 --> 17:03.131
[RUDEUS] Roxy! [grunts]

17:08.171 --> 17:09.211
[grunts]

17:18.811 --> 17:20.061
[sighs]

17:24.151 --> 17:26.021
[horse neighs]

17:27.901 --> 17:29.401
Take care, Highness.

17:29.531 --> 17:31.031
I do hope to see you again.

17:31.151 --> 17:33.701
You will. We'll meet again. Yes?

17:33.821 --> 17:36.491
You don't really have to go,
do you, Auntie Roxy?

17:36.621 --> 17:38.331
I still wanna learn magic
from you!

17:38.451 --> 17:40.291
-Yeah, sorry.
-Oh, wait.

17:40.411 --> 17:41.911
You could always
just join our party

17:42.041 --> 17:43.331
if you really wanted to.

17:43.461 --> 17:44.501
I appreciate the offer,

17:44.631 --> 17:46.131
but I'm satisfied
with my current job

17:46.251 --> 17:47.421
-at the university.
-[grumbles]

17:47.551 --> 17:50.011
-And my husband.
-Who cares about him?

17:50.131 --> 17:52.511
Besides, just think of how much
he's gonna spoil you

17:52.631 --> 17:54.891
when you finally get home
after months out on the road!

17:55.011 --> 17:57.601
[WOMAN] Alyssa! Leave her alone.

17:57.721 --> 17:59.311
Okay.

18:00.061 --> 18:01.271
[footsteps approaching]

18:01.811 --> 18:03.231
All right, we're off.

18:03.351 --> 18:04.481
I'll see you around.

18:04.601 --> 18:06.651
Yeah. You be safe.

18:06.771 --> 18:08.021
Back atcha.

18:08.231 --> 18:10.781
Your wives seem like they're
pretty close with each other.

18:10.901 --> 18:12.401
Don't you ever compare them.

18:12.531 --> 18:13.781
For sure.

18:13.901 --> 18:15.411
I will take that to heart.

18:15.531 --> 18:16.871
Great.

18:18.451 --> 18:19.831
See you.

18:25.291 --> 18:27.461
[♪ closing theme song playing]

18:29.751 --> 18:31.631
Rudy, are you positive

18:31.761 --> 18:33.671
you should have
just let her go like that?

18:33.801 --> 18:35.261
Um, what do you mean?

18:35.721 --> 18:36.891
Sara.

18:37.011 --> 18:39.561
You two used to have a thing,
didn't you?

18:40.811 --> 18:43.771
No, not exactly. We just...

18:44.271 --> 18:46.231
We were young and confused,

18:46.351 --> 18:48.191
and I was kind of stupid.

18:48.731 --> 18:50.901
Hmm. That's all?

18:51.861 --> 18:52.861
[giggles]

18:53.571 --> 18:56.281
Well then, tell me
about a girl you do like.

18:56.401 --> 18:57.451
Huh?

18:57.571 --> 19:00.331
Actually, yeah.
What's your type, Rudy?

19:03.001 --> 19:04.371
That's a good question.

19:04.831 --> 19:07.671
I think I like
women who swoop in

19:07.791 --> 19:10.251
to save me
whenever I'm in trouble.

19:10.381 --> 19:12.211
You don't say.

19:12.591 --> 19:14.011
[both chuckle]

19:14.131 --> 19:15.921
Well, goodness, Rudy,

19:16.051 --> 19:18.011
sounds like
we're pretty special to you.

19:18.141 --> 19:19.301
Yeah.

19:19.431 --> 19:20.931
You're my entire heart.

19:21.061 --> 19:22.061
[both chuckle]

19:22.221 --> 19:25.641
And special ladies
who sweep me off my feet,

19:25.771 --> 19:27.351
they're pretty rare.

19:27.981 --> 19:31.521
So yeah, you don't need
to play matchmaker with my exes.

19:31.981 --> 19:34.151
It's just the three of us
from here on out.

19:34.281 --> 19:35.781
I promise.

19:36.441 --> 19:38.661
Hmm. You say that now,

19:39.241 --> 19:41.991
but if someone is
truly special to you, Rudy,

19:42.121 --> 19:44.791
as long as they think
that you're special too,

19:45.371 --> 19:48.001
I want you to know
they're welcome in your heart.

19:48.121 --> 19:49.381
But who else?

19:52.591 --> 19:54.381
No, she ditched me.

19:55.171 --> 19:57.841
Although,
Ruijerd was pretty convinced

19:57.971 --> 19:59.841
that was all
a misunderstanding.

20:00.591 --> 20:02.181
[sighs]

20:02.681 --> 20:05.521
Okay. Well, I guess
you never know

20:05.641 --> 20:07.141
what the future holds,

20:07.271 --> 20:09.271
but I'll listen to my heart.

20:09.391 --> 20:10.481
[gasps softly]

20:10.901 --> 20:12.021
Got it.

20:12.941 --> 20:14.321
But if it happens,

20:14.401 --> 20:17.321
you had better bring her around
to meet us beforehand.

20:17.441 --> 20:19.321
I won't abide someone
trying to marry you

20:19.451 --> 20:20.411
if she doesn't love you,

20:20.951 --> 20:23.281
and that includes having love
and grace for your whole family.

20:23.411 --> 20:24.371
Sure.

20:24.871 --> 20:26.581
Just be honest with us.

20:26.701 --> 20:28.161
It should go without saying,

20:28.291 --> 20:30.921
but if I catch you
sneaking around with a mistress

20:31.041 --> 20:33.841
or any secret children,
we will have words.

20:33.961 --> 20:35.551
Yeah. Of course!

20:35.671 --> 20:36.671
[chuckles]

20:37.301 --> 20:40.931
Well, I look forward
to meeting number three someday.

20:41.051 --> 20:42.891
I know I'll love her.

20:44.561 --> 20:46.391
You're here
because your abilities

20:46.511 --> 20:48.681
have surpassed the level
of Sword Saint.

20:49.181 --> 20:52.691
And so, I think it's time
I named a new Sword King.

20:52.811 --> 20:54.731
But first, consider this.

20:54.861 --> 20:56.731
The Blade of Light
is the ultimate technique

20:56.861 --> 20:58.321
of the Sword God style,

20:58.441 --> 21:01.701
but its practitioners
still fall into different ranks.

21:01.821 --> 21:05.831
Saints, Kings, Emperors, God.

21:06.491 --> 21:08.121
What do you think
sets them apart?

21:08.251 --> 21:09.201
Gino?

21:09.331 --> 21:10.871
Well, it's not technique.

21:11.001 --> 21:13.421
Maybe it's their footwork
or their speed,

21:13.541 --> 21:16.421
or, um, how good
their weapons are might have--

21:16.551 --> 21:17.551
[GAL] Their weapons?!

21:17.671 --> 21:19.881
Are you trying
to embarrass yourself?

21:20.011 --> 21:21.721
Nope! No, I'm sorry, sir!

21:21.841 --> 21:24.221
Maybe you're just
a little too young to get it.

21:24.351 --> 21:25.601
That's fine.

21:25.721 --> 21:28.511
Don't gotta know everything
to be strong, kiddo.

21:29.021 --> 21:31.431
Nina, what do you think
sets them apart?

21:32.561 --> 21:33.851
Is it desire?

21:33.981 --> 21:35.151
Ha!

21:35.231 --> 21:37.821
Yeah, you have started
thinking about boys, huh?

21:38.441 --> 21:41.691
Okay. How does that desire fare
against any other?

21:42.151 --> 21:43.611
Pardon? I-- I don't--

21:44.071 --> 21:46.531
Say I told you that you could
either marry Gino,

21:46.661 --> 21:48.661
or you could become
a Sword King,

21:48.791 --> 21:50.081
but you couldn't do both.

21:50.201 --> 21:51.501
Which would you choose?

21:53.581 --> 21:55.171
To be a Sword King.

21:55.291 --> 21:56.461
[chuckles]

21:56.591 --> 21:58.751
You never did live
in the real world.

21:59.381 --> 22:01.421
'Kay, Eris, same question.

22:01.761 --> 22:02.761
It's resolve.

22:02.881 --> 22:04.221
Resolve, huh?

22:04.681 --> 22:06.551
I'm not so sure about that.

22:06.681 --> 22:08.931
[ERIS] I am. It's resolve.

22:09.061 --> 22:10.021
All right.

22:10.141 --> 22:12.141
So if I don't name you
Sword King--

22:12.271 --> 22:13.601
[ERIS] I won't really care.

22:14.101 --> 22:16.191
I thought you wanted
to get stronger.

22:16.311 --> 22:18.071
[ERIS] Yes, I do.

22:18.191 --> 22:20.151
But I couldn't care less
what people call me.

22:20.651 --> 22:21.941
[chuckles]

22:22.071 --> 22:24.321
Okay. Nina, Eris,

22:24.861 --> 22:27.571
winner will be granted
the title of Sword King.

22:28.081 --> 22:29.951
♪

22:31.041 --> 22:32.661
Takes you right back
to your first day

22:32.791 --> 22:34.121
at the dojo, doesn't it?

22:34.581 --> 22:35.711
[ERIS] Yeah.

22:35.831 --> 22:37.541
But today, I'm going to win.

22:40.001 --> 22:41.251
[gasps]

22:43.011 --> 22:44.801
Rudeus.

22:59.271 --> 23:00.941
[GAL] We gonna
stand around all day?

23:02.191 --> 23:03.441
[yells]

23:05.441 --> 23:07.201
[yelps, groans]

23:08.281 --> 23:09.331
All right!

23:09.831 --> 23:11.241
[groans]

23:11.371 --> 23:12.991
[panting]

23:14.291 --> 23:16.331
Frustrated, Nina?

23:16.961 --> 23:18.131
[NINA] Yes.

23:18.251 --> 23:19.751
You still have room to grow.

23:20.251 --> 23:21.711
Make the most of it.

23:22.711 --> 23:24.761
Yes. I will.

23:26.841 --> 23:28.091
Well done, Eris.

23:28.971 --> 23:31.891
I grant you the title
of Sword King.

23:32.011 --> 23:35.021
EPISODE 6
ANOTHER DOMESTIC DISASTER?

23:36.851 --> 23:40.021
NEXT TIME
PHASE FOUR
